  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Information :</strong> <a style=\"color: #ff0000;\" href=\"https://exams.nta.ac.in/AISSEE/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">National Testing Agency (NTA)</a></span> <span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">has released the Stage II Result for the Admission of National Institute of Fashion Technology NIFT 2026. </span>Applications for the NTA NIFT Online Form 2026 were accepted from December 08, 2025, to January 13, 2026. The online stage 2 examination <span data-teams=\"true\">was held on</span> 26 April 2026. Candidates who <span data-teams=\"true\">appeared for this examination can</span> can download their NTA NIFT Stage II Result 2026 from the link given below.</span></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-2\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n<script async=\"\" src=\"https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-1792973056979970\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" type=\"60786da3a9d6c8597d22a9e4-text/javascript\"></script>\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n<ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" style=\"display:block\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-1792973056979970\" data-ad-slot=\"4938044679\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\"></ins>\n<script type=\"60786da3a9d6c8597d22a9e4-text/javascript\">\n     (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});\n</script></div>\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">National Testing Agency (NTA)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">NTA NIFT Stage II Result 2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Notification Date : <strong>08 December 2025</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Application Start Date : <strong>08 December 2025</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Last Date : <strong>13 January 2026 (Extend)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">With Late Pay Exam Fee&nbsp;:&nbsp;<strong>14-16&nbsp;January 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Online Correction :&nbsp;<strong>18-19&nbsp;January 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Exam Date :<strong>&nbsp;08&nbsp;February 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Exam City Intimation:&nbsp;<strong>29 January 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Stage-I Admit Card : <strong>05</strong> <strong>February 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Stage-I Answer Key : <strong>17</strong> <strong>February 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Stage-I Result : <strong>20 March 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Final Answer Key : <strong>23 March 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Stage-II Exam Date :<strong> 26 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Stage-II Exam City Intimation : <strong>18 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Stage-II Admit Card : <strong>22 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Stage-II Result : <strong>03 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: #ffff00; color: #000000;\"><strong>Single Programmes</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General, OBC, EWS : <strong>Rs. 2000/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC, ST, PwD : <strong>Rs. 500/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: #ffff00; color: #000000;\"><strong>Both Programmes</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General, OBC, EWS : <strong>Rs. 3000/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC, ST, PwD : &nbsp;<strong>Rs. 750/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">NRI, OCI, Fore<a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"https://www.sarkaridisha.com/railway-rrb-ministerial-and-isolated-post-result/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">i</a>gn National / SAARC:&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Rs. 11100/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Late Fee Charge :&nbsp;<strong>Rs. 5000/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n<script async=\"\" src=\"https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-1792973056979970\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" type=\"60786da3a9d6c8597d22a9e4-text/javascript\"></script>\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n<ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" style=\"display:block\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-1792973056979970\" data-ad-slot=\"4938044679\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\"></ins>\n<script type=\"60786da3a9d6c8597d22a9e4-text/javascript\">\n     (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});\n</script></div>\n<p></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n<script async=\"\" src=\"https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-1792973056979970\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" type=\"60786da3a9d6c8597d22a9e4-text/javascript\"></script>\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n<ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" style=\"display:block\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-1792973056979970\" data-ad-slot=\"4938044679\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\"></ins>\n<script type=\"60786da3a9d6c8597d22a9e4-text/javascript\">\n     (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});\n</script></div>\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>NTA NIFT 2026 Notification : Age Limit</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Age Limit As On 01 August 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">B.Des &amp; B.F.Tech Maximum Age :<b> 24 Years</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">NIFT M.Des, M.F.M and M.F.Tech and PHd Courses : <strong>No Age Limit</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per NTA NIFT Online Form Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"><a style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\" href=\"https://sarkariresulttools.net/age-calculator/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><strong>Age Calculate</strong></a> </span>Tool – <a href=\"https://sarkariresulttools.net/age-calculator/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><strong>Click Here</strong></a></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>NTA NIFT Online Form 2026 : Exam Details</strong></span></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Exam Name : <span style=\"color: #000000;\">B.Des &amp; B.F.Tech &amp; M.Des, M.F.M and M.F.Tech and PHd</span></strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>NTA NIFT Online Form 2026 : Educational Qualification</b></span></h3>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.2753%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Exam Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 66.7247%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.2753%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">B.Des &amp; B.F.Tech</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 66.7247%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates Must Have Passed 10+2 Intermediate Exam in Any Recognized Board in India.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Appearing Candidate Also Eligible.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 33.2753%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">M.Des, M.F.M and M.F.Tech and PHd</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 66.7247%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates Having Under Graduate Degree in Any Recognized University / Institute in India.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Appearing Candidate Also Eligible.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>NIFT Online Form 2026 : </strong></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Mode of Selection</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Selection will be based on Online Examination</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>How To Download NTA NIFT Result 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">In order to download the NTA NIFT Result 2026 candidates need to go to the link provided below.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">After getting the link candidates need to click it for downloading their NTA NIFT Result 2026.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates will find the NTA NIFT Admit Card 2026 Page displaying.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">For Downloading their NTA NIFT Result 2026 Candidates will be redirected to the Login Page here they have provide their following details-:</span><br>\n<span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Registration Number</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Password/DOB</strong></span><br>\n<span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Click in the ‘Login’ Icon.</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates can also download their NTA NIFT Result 2026 from official site of the NTA.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n<script async=\"\" src=\"https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-1792973056979970\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" type=\"60786da3a9d6c8597d22a9e4-text/javascript\"></script>\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n<ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" style=\"display:block\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-1792973056979970\" data-ad-slot=\"493